- op: discuss  # 6c43
  at: '2026-11-13T08:54:01Z'  # 6c43
  by: agent  # 6c43
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6c43
  clock: 4  # 6c43
  nonce: 6c43  # 6c43
  message: "DONE in PR #2164 (dev e12978ccd5; code df9dbfaac7). ROOT CAUSE: a test that reads source files from disk imports none of them, so the import-graph slice cannot select it, and the only cover was one hand-written rule per gate. FIX (the derived list the item asks for): the read record the prose-only rule keeps says which tests read which files; for every changed .py file whose code changed, smart-test adds the test files recorded reading it (prose_only.tests_reading, coverage-select readers), above the manifest seam so merge CI runs them, and after narrowing so narrowing cannot drop them. Header line 'Read-record tests: N added'; --no-read-union turns it off; off in CI. THE ITEM'S OWN REPRO, re-run on a4e0bffecd with one statement appended to swift.py and BASE_BRANCH=HEAD: smart-test --manifest --no-read-union -> 378 test files, grep -c test_meta_key_coherence = 0; smart-test --manifest -> 414 test files, count = 1, header 'Read-record tests: 36 added'; the two lists differ by exactly those 36 and nothing was removed. Others among the 36: test_id_construction, test_producer_coherence, test_symbol_kinds, test_edge_types, test_evidence_types, test_test_only_reachability. BED (scripts/smart-test-bed, 20 edit scenarios, tests/test_tree_gate.py is this shape): MUST-select tests the manifest left out 29 before, 1 after (runtime dispatch, which only the local coverage union reaches); after narrowing 28 before, 0 after. TESTS: test_smart_test_read_union.py runs the shipped block (adds a reader, counts only its additions, never removes, a dead helper adds nothing, off switch, CI guard, position above the seam and after narrowing); test_prose_only.py pins tests_reading; test_smart_test_bed.py pins the gate in the manifest and narrowed stages and out of the static one. The WI-vosif hand rule for test_confidence_sites.py stays as a second cover. NOT ASSERTED: (1) a machine with no read record adds nothing until a run records one; (2) a test whose read happens in a process it starts is invisible to the recorder (364 test files start one; how many of them depend on source text is not measured), filed as the residual; (3) the first CI run of #2164 failed on the Python 3.11 side of one assertion (manifest == static when the prose rule gives way), fixed in e12978ccd5 and green on the re-run. ALSO FIXED in the PR: bed copies shared the installed hypergumbo's results cache and one could read a survey.json another was writing (slice failed, full-suite fallback, flaky stage sets); each copy now has its own XDG_CACHE_HOME and test_smart_test_prose_rule.py is grouped onto one xdist worker."  # 6c43
